{"name":"Cardinal Red","hex":"#9b365e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cardinal red","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bright red colour, between scarlet and crimson."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardinal_red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cardinal (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Cardinal is a vivid red, which may get its name from the cassocks worn by Catholic cardinals. The cardinal bird also takes its name from the cardinal bishops."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Northern_Cardinal_%28Cardinalis_cardinalis%29_male.jpg/330px-Northern_Cardinal_%28Cardinalis_cardinalis%29_male.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardinal_(color)","wikidata":"Q1426821"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Northern_Cardinal_-_bird_%28Cardinalis_cardinalis%29.JPG/500px-Northern_Cardinal_-_bird_%28Cardinalis_cardinalis%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Northern_Cardinal_-_bird_%28Cardi